Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:33:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/25] Modeling Algorithms - Corner of a convex and a concave
 fillet at a vertex with smooth edges

FreeCAD issue 20085, a cube of 20 with fillets of radius 6 and a square
hole of 8 x 8 whose walls go along the tangent lines of the fillets of
the cube: a lower edge of the hole (convex) and the vertical edge next to
it (concave) filleted together, the other lower edge at their vertex not.
The result was valid, but the corner was a plate patch with tolerance
0.38 (r = 1) to 1.1 (r = 2), visibly wavy.

On a vertex with three edges such a corner is built by
ChFi3d_FilBuilder::PerformTwoCorner: the fillets are cut where their
traces on their common face cross, and the corner is filled between the
two fillets and the other support of the fillet called OnSame. Here the
vertex also has smooth edges (between the fillets of the cube and its
sphere), so the ends of the spines are BreakPoint and the corner went to
PerformMoreThreeCorner.

- ChFi3d_TwoCornerInFacePlane: for two fillets from both sides of their
  common face whose traces on it cross, finds the fillet whose other
  support is a plane in which the other fillet ends (its last point on
  its other support lies on that plane, on an arc which does not bound
  the planar face): the concave fillet, whose other support is the next
  wall of the hole, where the convex fillet ends.
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformFilletOnVertex: such a corner of two fillets is
  given to PerformTwoCorner also on a vertex with more edges.
- ChFi3d_FilBuilder::PerformTwoCorner: with both ends BreakPoint, that
  fillet plays the OnSame one. The arc on which the other fillet ends is
  not an edge of the plane: the plane is extended up to that arc, and its
  piece from the end of the fillet to the vertex bounds the face beyond
  it, with the orientation of the arc in that face.

The 16 pairs of a vertical edge and a lower or upper edge next to it are
valid for r = 0.5 to 2.9 with tolerance 1e-4, with the same volume for
all of them (r = 1: 5157.00, r = 2: 5157.07 mm3).

New DRAW test bugs/modalg_8/fillet_rounded_cube_square_hole_convex_concave
and GTest
BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest.SquareHoleInRoundedCube_ConvexAndConcaveFilletsCorner.

